<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
        </smile>
        <name>IV Complex Non-Linear</name>
        <uuid>75259b6f-8c75-4bf3-9112-d1f2daf6e12d</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="Minutes" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>60</stop>
        <dt>0.25</dt>
        <isee:analyze_mode>false</isee:analyze_mode>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="model" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" link_high_level_map="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="1334" height="630" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="595" height="744" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="sector" />
    <model>
        <stock name="Heat_Available">
            <doc>This value was chosen to meet the needs of the final model.</doc>
            <eqn>210000&#x0D;{Joules}</eqn>
            <outflow>Heat_Loss</outflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="170" y="137" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Heat_Loss">
            <doc>This scenario depends on the difference between the temperatures of the coffee and the the surrounding room.  AS the coffee temperature falls closer and closer to the room temperature, less and less heat will be lost, until the two temperatures are equal and no net heat transfer takes place.&#x0D;&#x0D;EDITORS&apos; NOTE:  If a biflow (say labelled, &quot;Heat Change&quot;) were used, a situation in which room temperature exceeded the coffee would result in warming the cup.</doc>
            <eqn>Temperature_Gap * 100&#x0D;{Joules per minute}</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="265" y="132" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="85">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="190" y="132" />
                    <pt x="340" y="132" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Coffee_Temperature">
            <doc>This is a bit convoluted but it provides an initial energy content of the coffee (104,600 Joules) so that, when divided by the specific heat of water (4.184 Joules/gram * degree centigrade) and the massof 1 cup of coffee (250 grams), the initial temperature is 100 degrees centigrade.</doc>
            <eqn>(Heat_Available - 105400)/(4.184*250)&#x0D;{Degrees centigrade}</eqn>
            <display x="201" y="223" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Room_Temperature">
            <doc>This is the conventional value for room temperature.</doc>
            <eqn>25&#x0D;{degrees centigrade}</eqn>
            <display x="361" y="223" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Temperature_Gap">
            <eqn>Coffee_Temperature-Room_Temperature</eqn>
            <display x="280" y="193" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <display page_width="595" page_height="744" isee:converter_size="large" interval="DT">
            <connector x="163" y="152" uid="0">
                <from>Heat_Available</from>
                <to>Coffee_Temperature</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="205" y="212" uid="1">
                <from>Coffee_Temperature</from>
                <to>Temperature_Gap</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="352" y="216" uid="2">
                <from>Room_Temperature</from>
                <to>Temperature_Gap</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="285" y="182" uid="3">
                <from>Temperature_Gap</from>
                <to>Heat_Loss</to>
            </connector>
            <stacked_container x="44" y="284" height="282" width="492" uid="4">
                <graph type="time_series" title="Untitled" background="#C8C8C8" show_grid="true" plot_numbers="true" isee:use_five_segments="false" date_time="2025-02-04T09:46:50Z" cleared="true" time_precision="2" from="0" to="60">
                    <plot index="0" pen_width="1" color="red" precision="0.01" show_y_axis="true">
                        <scale min="-50" max="100" />
                        <entity name="Coffee_Temperature" />
                    </plot>
                    <plot index="1" pen_width="1" color="blue" precision="0.01" show_y_axis="true">
                        <scale min="-50" max="100" />
                        <entity name="Room_Temperature" />
                    </plot>
                </graph>
            </stacked_container>
            <pad_icon x="166" y="439" width="26" height="22" color="fuchsia" label_side="bottom" label="Graph 1" type="graph" icon_of="4" />
            <text_box x="64" y="1" uid="5" color="#7F00FF" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="459" height="61">COOLING COFFEE II&#x0D;Model to Accompany Powers&apos;&#x0D;IV.  Non-Linear Heat Loss Regulated by the Temperature Gap&#x0D;</text_box>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        </display>
        <interface page_cols="0" page_rows="0" page_width="1588" page_height="1128" home_page="0">
            <simulation_delay>0</simulation_delay>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        </interface>
        <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </model>
</xmile>
